nvolves moving 30 big cats that spent years in cramped cages and suffered health problems. The animals will now travel to Lionsrock in South Africa and The Wild Animal Sanctuary in Colorado.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/30-lions-and-tigers-spent-years-in-cramped-concrete-cages-at-a-notorious-argentine-zoo-they-are-now-beginning-a-journey-to-sanctuaries-where-they-can-finally-roam-freely/articleshow/133295851.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/30-lions-and-tigers-spent-years-in-cramped-concrete-cages-at-a-notorious-argentine-zoo-they-are-now-beginning-a-journey-to-sanctuaries-where-they-can-finally-roam-freely/articleshow/133295851.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-17T22:06:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133298371,imgsize-119602.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Only nine such butterflies were found in US in 2022; 3 years later, over 1,300 were released]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133273631.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Researchers in Michigan have helped bring the Poweshiek skipperling butterfly back from the brink of extinction after its US wild population fell to just nine in 2022. Through captive breeding, habitat restoration and carefully planned releases, more than 1,300 butterflies were released in 2025. The recovery effort has now expanded to other endangered butterflies, while restored prairie habitats are helping support wider ecosystems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/only-nine-of-these-butterflies-were-found-across-the-us-in-2022-three-years-later-researchers-released-more-than-1300-to-rebuild-the-species/articleshow/133273631.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[htt